{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מאהל", :translit "me'ohel", :gloss "from [the] tent"} {:he "ד' במסורה", :translit "dalet ba-mesorah", :gloss "four in the Masorah"} {:he "ויצא מאהל לאה", :translit "vayetze me'ohel le'ah", :gloss "and he went out from the tent of Leah"} {:he "מאהל מועד לאמר", :translit "me'ohel mo'ed leimor", :gloss "from the tent of meeting, saying"} {:he "ואהיה מתהלך מאהל אל אהל", :translit "veh'yeiti mithalech me'ohel el ohel", :gloss "and I will walk from tent to tent"} {:he "יתצך לנצח ויסחך מאהל", :translit "yatzatzecha lanetzach veyisachecha me'ohel", :gloss "I will cut you off forever and uproot you from [the] tent"} {:he "בשעה שהוקם המשכן נאסרו הבמות", :translit "be'sha'ah shehukam ha-mishkan ne'esru ha-bamot", :gloss "at the time that the Tabernacle was established the high places were forbidden"} {:he "ולאחר שעברו הירדן הותרו הבמות עד שבאו לשילה", :translit "vele'achar she'avru ha-yarden hutru ha-bamot ad sheba'u le-shiloh", :gloss "and after they crossed the Jordan the high places were permitted until they came to Shiloh"} {:he "ואז נאסרו הבמות", :translit "ve'az ne'esru ha-bamot", :gloss "and then the high places were forbidden"} {:he "שלא היה שום היתר", :translit "shelo haya shum hetter", :gloss "that there was no permit at all"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["ויצא מאהל לאה" "מאהל מועד לאמר" "ואהיה מתהלך מאהל אל אהל" "יתצך לנצח ויסחך מאהל"]} {:kind :other, :note "Four occurrences of מאהל are read as four historical stages of the Tabernacle's location, mapping each verse to a phase of the halakhic status of במות (high places)."}], :frame {:text "The halakhic status of במות (high places) depends on whether the Tabernacle or Temple is established. Before the Tabernacle was erected, במות were permitted. Once it was erected, they were forbidden. After crossing the Jordan and before arriving at Shiloh, they were permitted again. At Shiloh they were forbidden. When the Tabernacle moved from Shiloh to Nov and then to Givon, במות were permitted again during those interim periods. Once the Eternal House (the Temple in Jerusalem) was built, במות were forbidden permanently with no further permit. The Tribe of Judah descended from Leah; Joseph descended from Rachel. Bezalel came from the Tribe of Judah. Shiloh was located in the territory of Joseph (Ephraim). The Rosh is the title of Rabbi Asher ben Yechiel (c. 1250–1327), whom the Ba'al HaTurim calls 'my lord my father.'", :sources ["Zevachim 112b-113a" "Zevachim 117b" "Genesis 29:35" "Genesis 30:24" "Exodus 31:2" "Joshua 18:1" "1 Samuel 21:1-6" "1 Kings 6:1-2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["ויצא מאהל לאה" "מאהל מועד לאמר" "ואהיה מתהלך מאהל אל אהל" "יתצך לנצח ויסחך מאהל"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויצא מאהל לאה", :refs ["Genesis 31:33"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "מאהל מועד לאמר", :refs ["Leviticus 1:1"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ואהיה מתהלך מאהל אל אהל", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "יתצך לנצח ויסחך מאהל", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Four occurrences of מאהל are read as four historical stages of the Tabernacle's location, mapping each verse to a phase of the halakhic status of במות (high places).", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:09:35.303701985Z", :model "glm-5.2"}